Milvus 3.0.3 security rebuild
Upstream: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/tree/328df0cd2f323c2d3c50cef91bfc9f2c412bcb09
License: Apache-2.0; upstream copyright and dependency licenses remain applicable.

Daydream rebuilds the Go main binary and Go planparser library using Go 1.26.10
and the adjacent dependency locks. The planparser C++ bridge is recompiled from
the same source. Other native libraries are unchanged from the pinned official
3.0.3 image. This is not an upstream Milvus release or a claim of zero defects.

The Dockerfile pins all source/header downloads by SHA-256. It provides the
exact source URLs, and the adjacent go.mod/go.sum files record our dependency
changes. The application module is independent of these rebuild dependencies.

Avro's archived github.com/hamba/avro/v2 is replaced with the maintained MIT
fork github.com/iskorotkov/avro/v2 v2.33.0 (GO-2026-5046/5047/5048 fixes).
Its public crc64 helper is locked at v2.34.0. The fork's LICENCE and the original
Hamba copyright/permission notice are both retained. Pulsar and Milvus keep their
existing APIs and snapshot format; the replacement changes the decoder code.
